cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use REFORGE in research or in a product, cite it like this."
title: "REFORGE: reverse-engineer any AI image or video into a reproducible recipe"
abstract: >-
  REFORGE recovers or reconstructs the generation parameters behind AI-generated media.
  It reads embedded metadata first (A1111, ComfyUI, NovelAI, InvokeAI, EXIF, MP4, C2PA),
  falls back to structured captioning and control-map extraction, and packages the result
  as a versioned recipe (prompt, sampling pins, control signals, reference images,
  inversion latents) that is stamped back into the file. A model-free metric suite
  (PSNR, SSIM, DCT-pHash, edge IoU, palette delta) grades every regenerated result on an
  L0-L3 fidelity scale, so "reproducible" is measured rather than asserted.
authors:
  - name: "REFORGE contributors"
    website: "https://github.com/zhangbotong92-cyber/reforge"
version: "0.3.1"
date-released: "2026-11-18"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/zhangbotong92-cyber/reforge"
url: "https://github.com/zhangbotong92-cyber/reforge"
keywords:
  - prompt reverse engineering
  - image-to-prompt
  - reproducibility
  - diffusion inversion
  - content provenance
  - C2PA
  - ComfyUI
  - video generation
